# Origin: legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/maths-errors.chk
# Milestone: M6 Wave 2 (Phase 11 partial port)
#
# Legacy fixture asserts:
#   - `1 / 0` raises `/: division by 0` — v0.13.5 now CONFORMS:
#     the zero divisor raises a catchable DivByZero.  The earlier v1.0
#     IEEE-754 `inf` divergence is closed (legacy urbi is all-Float and
#     float.cc checks `if (!rhs) RAISE("division by 0")`).
#   - `Math.sqrt(-10.0) / log(-10.0) / acos(-100.0) / asin(-100.0)`
#     raise domain-specific diagnostics — v0.6.1 has no Math.sqrt /
#     log / acos / asin (Math has only constants pi/e/nan/infinity).
#   - `Math.sqr("foo")` raises `sqr: lookup failed: sqr` — v1.0 also
#     raises a sqr lookup failure but via the Float atom-proto fallback.
#
# This port keeps the legacy file's "lookup failure on missing Math
# slot" assertion (the only one that remains semantically sharp at
# v1.0) and the now-conformant div-by-zero raise.
#
# Wave-2 deferred (full port): all Math.{sqrt,log,acos,asin,sqr}
# methods + their domain-error diagnostics.  See PORT_NOTES.md.

# `1 / 0` raises DivByZero at v0.13.5, matching legacy
# `/: division by 0`.  Conformance closed.
1 / 0
[00000000] !!! line 1: DivByZero: division by 0

# Math at v0.6.1 ships constants only; method lookups fail as
# `slot 'NAME' not found` via the SELF proto-walk diagnostic.
#
# NOTE (v0.11.4): the slot-not-found TypeError is now a CATCHABLE typed
# throw (see tests/chk/exceptions/vm_typeerror_catchable.chk) rather than a
# fatal HALT.  Uncaught at the REPL surface it surfaces the instance `message`
# slot as the legacy "!!! TypeError: ..." diagnostic (D-F2 backward-compat).
Math.sqrt(4)
[00000001] !!! TypeError: method call: slot 'sqrt' not found

Math.log(1)
[00000002] !!! TypeError: method call: slot 'log' not found

Math.sqr(2)
[00000003] !!! TypeError: method call: slot 'sqr' not found

# Math.nan exists; Math.nan.isNaN() routes through the Float atom-
# proto installed at Phase 5.
Math.nan.isNaN()
[00000004] true
